	// b = (a & b) + (b only bits) = am + complement subset of x's bits
	// Since am >= 0 and x >= 0, and a, b are positive:
	// a = am + p, b = am + (x - p) where p is a submask of x.
	// a > 0 and b > 0.
	// Since am = (s-x)/2 and s >= 2, x >= 0.
	// If am == 0, then a = p, b = x - p. We need p > 0 and x - p > 0.
	// If am > 0, then a = am + p >= am > 0, and b = am + (x-p) >= am > 0, so always positive.

	result := int64(1)
